      "problem": "Simplify $6{(\\frac{2a}{3})}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{(\\frac{2a}{3})}^{3}=6\\cdot \\frac{(2a)^{3}}{{3}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot \\frac{(2a)^{3}}{{3}^{3}} & = \\\\ 6\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{3}{a}^{3}}{{3}^{3}} & = \\\\ 6\\cdot \\frac{8{a}^{3}}{27} & = \\\\ \\frac{48{a}^{3}}{27} & = \\\\ \\frac{16{a}^{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
